+ − Fit ⛶ DagreForceCircle ConcentricTreeGrid LOD L0 · classes only L1 · + hierarchy L2 · + individuals &amp; object props L3 · + OWL restrictions L4 · + data props &amp; literals L5 · everything except inferred L6 · everything Hidden  Group Facets Style: Ontoink Style: Chowlk Style: Graffoo Style: VOWL PNG SVG TTL Edit Layout Abstract Stats Paths SPARQL Reasoning Edit &amp; Validate Hidden by LOD  ·  pin to reveal× Facets  ·  narrow the view× Suggested SHACL shapes× Cite this ontology× Inferred Triples (OWL-RL)×  Show on graph Validate with Inferences Edit &amp; Validate× Source (data TTL) SHACL Shapes Validation Report Validate Update Graph Reset <p>RDF data:</p> <pre><code>@prefix ex: &lt;https://www.example.org/&gt; .
@prefix owl: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#&gt; .
@prefix rdf: &lt;http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&gt; .
@prefix rdfs: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt; .

@prefix lp: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/&gt; .

# Klassen
@prefix Lehrplan: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000438&gt; .
@prefix Titel: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000346&gt; .

# Instanzen
@prefix sachsen: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_3000047&gt; .
@prefix mathematik_sn: &lt;https://w3id.org/schulfach/SN_0000012&gt; .
@prefix oberschule_sn: &lt;https://w3id.org/schulart/SN_0000003&gt; .
@prefix sekundarbereich_ii: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000046&gt; .

# properties
@prefix hat_titel: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030056&gt; .
@prefix von_bundesland: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000029&gt; .
@prefix hat_schulfach: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000537&gt; .
@prefix fuer_schulart: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000812&gt;.
@prefix hat_schulstufe: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000047&gt;.
@prefix hat_wert: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000344&gt; .

ex:lehrplan_1 a Lehrplan: ;
            hat_titel: ex:titel_1 ;
            von_bundesland: sachsen: ;
            hat_schulfach: mathematik_sn: ;
            fuer_schulart: oberschule_sn: ;
            hat_schulstufe: sekundarbereich_ii: . 

ex:titel_1 a Titel: ;
        hat_wert:  "Lehrplan Oberschule Mathematik" .
</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>Curriculum (Lehrplan, <code>LP_0000438</code>) is the common superclass of all curricula. Each state-specific designation is a subclass of it: LehrplanPLUS (BY), Bildungsplan (BW, HB, HH), Kernlehrplan (NW), Kerncurriculum (NI, HE), Rahmenlehrplan (BE, BB), Rahmenplan (MV), Fachanforderung (SH) and Lehrplan (RP, SL, SN, ST, TH) (the curriculum types of the individual states, e.g. framework curriculum or core curriculum).</p> <p>Contextualization information</p> <p>A curriculum carries the information that describes its institutional scope:</p> <ul> <li>of federal state (von Bundesland, <code>LP_0000029</code>) → the issuing state, e.g. Bayern (Bavaria, <code>LP_3000051</code>)</li> <li>for type of school (für Schulart, <code>LP_0000812</code>) → the school type for which the curriculum applies, e.g. Grundschule (primary school, <code>schulart:BY_0000001</code>)</li> <li>has educational track level (hat Bildungsgangniveau, <code>LP_0000833</code>) → alternatively or additionally the educational track level, e.g. Realschulniveau (BY) (Realschule level, Bavaria, <code>LP_0000030</code>)</li> <li>has school subject (hat Schulfach, <code>LP_0000537</code>) → the school subject, e.g. Sport (physical education, <code>schulfach:BY_0000013</code>)</li> <li>has class level (hat Jahrgangsstufe, <code>LP_0000026</code>) → the class levels for which the curriculum applies</li> <li>has educational level (hat Schulstufe, <code>LP_0000047</code>) → alternatively or additionally the superordinate educational level, e.g. Primarbereich (primary level, <code>LP_0000036</code>)</li> </ul> <p>Together, this information makes a curriculum uniquely identifiable: „Bayern – Grundschule – Sport – Jahrgangsstufen 1 und 2“ (Bavaria – primary school – physical education – class levels 1 and 2).</p> <p>Further information</p> <ul> <li>has title (hat Titel, <code>LP_0030056</code>) → the official title as a title individual (see Pattern 2)</li> <li>has description (hat Beschreibung, <code>LP_0030051</code>) → an explanatory text as a description individual</li> <li>uri (<code>LP_0000463</code>) → the Uniform Resource Locator (URL) of the original document at the publisher, e.g. on the state's school portal</li> <li>has direct part (hat direkten Teil, <code>LP_0000565</code>) → the top structural level of the curriculum (see Pattern 6)</li> <li>veröffentlicht am (published on) and has validity scope (hat Gültigkeitsbereich) → temporal information (see Pattern 13)</li> </ul>

+ − Fit ⛶ DagreForceCircle ConcentricTreeGrid LOD L0 · classes only L1 · + hierarchy L2 · + individuals &amp; object props L3 · + OWL restrictions L4 · + data props &amp; literals L5 · everything except inferred L6 · everything Hidden  Group Facets Style: Ontoink Style: Chowlk Style: Graffoo Style: VOWL PNG SVG TTL Edit Layout Abstract Stats Paths SPARQL Reasoning Edit &amp; Validate Hidden by LOD  ·  pin to reveal× Facets  ·  narrow the view× Suggested SHACL shapes× Cite this ontology× Inferred Triples (OWL-RL)×  Show on graph Validate with Inferences Edit &amp; Validate× Source (data TTL) SHACL Shapes Validation Report Validate Update Graph Reset <p>RDF data:</p> <pre><code>@prefix ex: &lt;https://www.example.org/&gt; .
@prefix owl: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#&gt; .
@prefix rdf: &lt;http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&gt; .
@prefix rdfs: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt; .

@prefix lp: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/&gt; .

# Klassen
@prefix Bildungsplan_BW: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000806&gt; .
@prefix Lehrplanfragment_BW: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0002052&gt; .
@prefix Titel: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000346&gt; .
@prefix Beschreibung: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030003&gt; .
@prefix Identifikationsnummer: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000347&gt; .
@prefix Kompetenzbereich_BW: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030174&gt; .


# properties
@prefix hat_titel: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030056&gt; .
@prefix hat_direkten_teil: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000565&gt; .
@prefix hat_position: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000460&gt; .
@prefix hat_nummer: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030057&gt; .
@prefix hat_beschreibung: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030051&gt; .
@prefix hat_wert: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000344&gt; .

ex:lehrplan_1 a Bildungsplan_BW: ;
            hat_direkten_teil: ex:fragment_1 ;
            hat_titel: ex:titel_1 .
ex:fragment_1 a Lehrplanfragment_BW: ;
            hat_direkten_teil: ex:bereich_1 ;
            hat_position: 1 ;
            hat_titel: ex:titel_2 .

ex:bereich_1  a Kompetenzbereich_BW: ;
            hat_position: 1 ;
            hat_titel: ex:titel_3 ;
            hat_nummer: ex:nummer_1 ;
            hat_beschreibung: ex:beschreibung_1 .

ex:titel_1 a Titel: ;
    hat_wert: "Bildungsplan Sekundarstufe I - Deutsch" .

ex:titel_2 a Titel: ;
    hat_wert: "Prozessbezogene Kompetenzen" .

ex:titel_3 a Titel: ;
    hat_wert: "Sprechen und Zuhören" .


ex:beschreibung_1 a Beschreibung: ;
    hat_wert: "Die Schülerinnen und Schüler erwerben kommunikative Kompetenz ..."  .

ex:nummer_1 a Identifikationsnummer: ;
    hat_wert: "2.1" .
</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>The texts of a curriculum are not attached to the elements as simple literals but modeled as separate information units. The actual text is attached to this individual via has value (hat Wert, <code>LP_0000344</code>).</p> <p>Title (Titel, <code>LP_0000346</code>) – property: has title (<code>LP_0030056</code>)</p> <p>A title carries the designation of an element as it appears in the printed or digital curriculum. It is not identical to the <code>rdfs:label</code> of the element: the label is a caption for display, whereas the title reproduces the original text of the document. has title can be used on curricula and on curricular elements (domain: curricular element (Curriculares Element) or curriculum). For a competency specification (CE-Kompetenzspezifikation), a title is part of the definition.</p> <p>Description (Beschreibung, <code>LP_0030003</code>) – property: has description (<code>LP_0030051</code>)</p> <p>The description carries longer, explanatory texts: explanations of competence areas, methodological notes, didactic comments, examples of concretization or texts on the educational mission. has description can also be used on curricula and curricular elements.</p> <p>ID number (Identifikationsnummer, <code>LP_0000347</code>) – property: has number (hat Nummer, <code>LP_0030057</code>)</p> <p>The ID number preserves the numbering of the original document, e.g. „3.1“, „LB 2“ or „A.1“. It is intended only for curricular elements (domain: curricular element). Since the IRIs of the elements are unique but not human-readable (e.g. <code>https://w3id.org/lehrplan/resource/by/a0010229-…</code>), the number establishes the link to the corresponding place in the original document.</p> <p>Structure and order</p> <p>The example also shows how elements are nested within each other: via has direct part (<code>LP_0000565</code>) an element refers to its immediate parts, and via hat Position (has position, <code>LP_0000460</code>) the order of the parts within their parent element is recorded.</p> <pre><code>Curriculares Element
  ├─[hat Titel]──────────▶ Titel                  → Name des Elements im Dokument
  ├─[hat Nummer]─────────▶ Identifikationsnummer  → z. B. "3.1" oder "LB 2"
  ├─[hat Beschreibung]───▶ Beschreibung           → erläuternder Text
  └─[hat Position]───────▶ 1, 2, 3 …              → Reihenfolge im Elternelement
</code></pre>

+ − Fit ⛶ DagreForceCircle ConcentricTreeGrid LOD L0 · classes only L1 · + hierarchy L2 · + individuals &amp; object props L3 · + OWL restrictions L4 · + data props &amp; literals L5 · everything except inferred L6 · everything Hidden  Group Facets Style: Ontoink Style: Chowlk Style: Graffoo Style: VOWL PNG SVG TTL Edit Layout Abstract Stats Paths SPARQL Reasoning Edit &amp; Validate Hidden by LOD  ·  pin to reveal× Facets  ·  narrow the view× Suggested SHACL shapes× Cite this ontology× Inferred Triples (OWL-RL)×  Show on graph Validate with Inferences Edit &amp; Validate× Source (data TTL) SHACL Shapes Validation Report Validate Update Graph Reset <p>RDF data:</p> <pre><code>@prefix ex: &lt;https://www.example.org/&gt; .
@prefix owl: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#&gt; .
@prefix rdf: &lt;http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&gt; .
@prefix rdfs: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt; .

@prefix lp: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/&gt; .

# Klassen
@prefix Schulfach: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000001&gt; .
@prefix Fremdsprachenfach: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000004&gt; .
@prefix Schulfachbezug: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000540&gt; .
@prefix Erste_Fremdsprache: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000541&gt; .

# Instanzen
@prefix englisch_th: &lt;https://w3id.org/schulfach/TH_0000006&gt; .
@prefix griechisch_st: &lt;https://w3id.org/schulfach/ST_0000014&gt; .
@prefix englisch_kim_schulfach: &lt;http://w3id.org/kim/schulfaecher/s1007&gt; .

# properties
@prefix hat_schulfach: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000537&gt; .
@prefix has_exact_match: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch&gt; .

ex:lehrplan_1 hat_schulfach: 
                           ex:fachbezug_englisch_als_erstsprache_1 .
ex:fachbezug_englisch_als_erstsprache_1 hat_schulfach: englisch_th: ;
                                      a Erste_Fremdsprache: .

ex:lehrplan_2 hat_schulfach: griechisch_st: .

griechisch_st: a Schulfach: .

englisch_th: a Schulfach: ;
             has_exact_match: englisch_kim_schulfach: .
englisch_kim_schulfach: a Fremdsprachenfach: .
Fremdsprachenfach: rdfs:subClassOf Schulfach: .
Erste_Fremdsprache: rdfs:subClassOf Schulfachbezug: .
</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>The example shows two curricula: one is directly assigned a school subject, the other a school subject property.</p> <p>School subject (Schulfach, <code>LP_0000001</code>) is the class of all school subjects. For frequently queried groups of subjects there are subclasses:</p> <ul> <li>MINT-Fach (STEM subject, <code>LP_0000002</code>; MINT: Mathematik, Informatik, Naturwissenschaften und Technik, i.e. mathematics, computer science, natural sciences and technology) with the subclass Naturwissenschaftsfach (natural science subject, <code>LP_0000003</code>)</li> <li>Fremdsprachenfach (foreign language subject, <code>LP_0000004</code>)</li> <li>Gesellschaftswissenschaftsfach (social science subject, <code>LP_0000005</code>)</li> <li>BistaFach (<code>LP_0000039</code>) for the subjects for which there are KMK educational standards (KMK: Standing Conference of the Ministers of Education and Cultural Affairs, Kultusministerkonferenz)</li> </ul> <p>The concrete subjects come from the school subject ontology (<code>https://w3id.org/schulfach</code>): 898 subjects, one per state and subject name, e.g. <code>schulfach:BY_0000001</code> (Deutsch/German), <code>schulfach:HH_0000004</code> (Deutsch), <code>schulfach:SN_0000001</code> (Deutsch). The fact that the same subject is a separate individual in each state reflects reality: the names differ from one another, e.g. Arbeit-Wirtschaft-Technik, AWT or Arbeitslehre (variants of a work/economics/technology subject). For 733 subjects there is a <code>skos:exactMatch</code> and for 51 a <code>skos:closeMatch</code> to the nationwide KIM school subject vocabulary (KIM-Schulfachvokabular; KIM: Kompetenzzentrum Interoperable Metadaten, competence center for interoperable metadata), which serves as a common reference point for cross-state queries.</p> <p>In the curriculum data, a subject is linked to a curriculum via has school subject (<code>LP_0000537</code>).</p> <p>School subject property (Schulfachbezug, <code>LP_0000540</code>) describes the status of a subject in a particular context:</p> <ul> <li>Pflichtfach (compulsory subject, <code>LP_0000544</code>): mandatory for all students</li> <li>Wahlpflichtfach (compulsory elective subject, <code>LP_0000545</code>): mandatory choice from a fixed offering</li> <li>Wahlfach (elective subject, <code>LP_0000551</code>): optional</li> <li>Erste, Zweite and Dritte Fremdsprache (first, second and third foreign language, <code>LP_0000541</code>, <code>LP_0000542</code>, <code>LP_0000543</code>)</li> </ul> <p>A school subject property in turn refers to the subject via has school subject. Therefore has school subject allows both school subject and school subject property as its range. This is particularly important for foreign languages: depending on the state and educational track, English can be the first, second or third foreign language – each with different requirements. This makes it possible, for example, to query all curricula for "English as a second foreign language" nationwide.</p>

+ − Fit ⛶ DagreForceCircle ConcentricTreeGrid LOD L0 · classes only L1 · + hierarchy L2 · + individuals &amp; object props L3 · + OWL restrictions L4 · + data props &amp; literals L5 · everything except inferred L6 · everything Hidden  Group Facets Style: Ontoink Style: Chowlk Style: Graffoo Style: VOWL PNG SVG TTL Edit Layout Abstract Stats Paths SPARQL Reasoning Edit &amp; Validate Hidden by LOD  ·  pin to reveal× Facets  ·  narrow the view× Suggested SHACL shapes× Cite this ontology× Inferred Triples (OWL-RL)×  Show on graph Validate with Inferences Edit &amp; Validate× Source (data TTL) SHACL Shapes Validation Report Validate Update Graph Reset <p>RDF data:</p> <pre><code>@prefix ex: &lt;https://www.example.org/&gt; .
@prefix owl: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#&gt; .
@prefix rdf: &lt;http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&gt; .
@prefix rdfs: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt; .

@prefix lp: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/&gt; .

# Klassen
@prefix Schulart: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000111&gt; .
@prefix Hauptschulniveau: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000834&gt; .
@prefix Gymnasialniveau_Sek_II: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000835&gt; .

# Instanzen
@prefix integrierte_gesamtschule_rp: &lt;https://w3id.org/schulart/RP_0000002&gt; .
@prefix gesamtschule_kim: &lt;https://w3id.org/kim/schularten/s05&gt; .
@prefix rheinland_pfalz: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_3000046&gt; .
@prefix jahrgangsstufe_9: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_2000009&gt; .
@prefix grundlegendes_kompetenzniveau_rp: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000147&gt; .
@prefix niveau_sekundarstufe_ii_rp: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030353&gt; .

# properties
@prefix has_exact_match: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch&gt; .
@prefix von_bundesland: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000029&gt; .
@prefix hat_jahrgangsstufe: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000026&gt; .
@prefix hat_bildungsgangniveau: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000833&gt; .

integrierte_gesamtschule_rp: a Schulart: ;
                          has_exact_match: gesamtschule_kim: ;
                          von_bundesland: rheinland_pfalz: ;
                          hat_jahrgangsstufe: jahrgangsstufe_9: ;
                          hat_bildungsgangniveau: grundlegendes_kompetenzniveau_rp: ,
                                                  niveau_sekundarstufe_ii_rp: .
grundlegendes_kompetenzniveau_rp: a Hauptschulniveau: .
niveau_sekundarstufe_ii_rp: a Gymnasialniveau_Sek_II: .
</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>School type (Schulart, <code>LP_0000111</code>) describes a form of school. The school type ontology comprises 89 school types from all 16 states – one for each state-specifically named form of school. A school type is an information unit; the role that a concrete school has as a school of this type is the school type role (Schulartfunktion).</p> <p>Only Grundschule (primary school) and Gymnasium (academic secondary school) exist under the same name in all states. The other school types differ in part considerably: the Mittelschule in Bavaria corresponds, for example, to the Regelschule in Thuringia, the Regionale Schule in Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, the Oberschule in Saxony or the Hauptschule in Lower Saxony. As an integrated form of school, Hamburg has only the Stadtteilschule, Schleswig-Holstein the Gemeinschaftsschule, while North Rhine-Westphalia distinguishes between Gesamtschule and Sekundarschule.</p> <p>Each school type is assigned to a state via of federal state (<code>LP_0000029</code>) and has a state-specific IRI, e.g. <code>schulart:RP_0000002</code> (Integrierte Gesamtschule, integrated comprehensive school in Rhineland-Palatinate). Curricula refer via for type of school (<code>LP_0000812</code>) to the school type for which they apply.</p>

