@prefix owl: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#&gt; .
@prefix rdf: &lt;http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&gt; .
@prefix rdfs: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt; .

@prefix lp: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/&gt; .

# Klassen
@prefix Lehrplan: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000438&gt; .
@prefix CE_Fragment: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0001015&gt; .
@prefix CE_Bereich: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000349&gt; .
@prefix CE_Lerninhalt: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000332&gt; .
@prefix CE_Kompetenzspezifikation: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000263&gt; .
@prefix CE_Hinweis: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000852&gt; .

# properties
@prefix hat_direkten_teil: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000565&gt; .

ex:lehrplan_1 hat_direkten_teil: ex:ce_fragment_1 .
ex:ce_fragment_1 hat_direkten_teil: ex:ce_bereich_1 .
ex:ce_bereich_1 hat_direkten_teil: ex:ce_bereich_2 .
ex:ce_bereich_2 hat_direkten_teil: ex:ce_lerninhalt_1 ,
                          ex:ce_kompetenzspezifikation_1 .                   
ex:ce_lerninhalt_1 hat_direkten_teil: ex:ce_lerninhalt_2 .
ex:ce_lerninhalt_2 hat_direkten_teil: ex:ce_hinweis_1 .
ex:ce_kompetenzspezifikation_1 hat_direkten_teil: ex:ce_hinweis_2 .
</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>Curricular elements (Curriculare Elemente, <code>LP_0000261</code>) are the building blocks from which a curriculum is constructed. Every information unit of a curriculum – a chapter, a competence area, an individual requirement, a learning content – is a curricular element. The generic subclasses carry the prefix CE- in their German labels:</p> <p>Fragment (CE-Fragment) is a purely structuring component: chapters, sections and headings that structure a curriculum without themselves describing competences or content. Each state has its own class for this, e.g. Lehrplanfragment (BY) (curriculum fragment, Bavaria).</p> <p>Area (CE-Bereich) groups competences and learning content under a common subject-related focus and can be superordinate or subordinate to other areas. The names used by the states range from Kompetenzbereich (competence area) via Lernbereich (learning area), Leitidee (guiding idea) and Themenfeld (topic area) to Inhaltsfeld (content field).</p> <p>Competency specification (CE-Kompetenzspezifikation) describes a concrete competence – typically as a sentence with an operator that begins with "Die Schülerinnen und Schüler …" ("Students …"). The ontology distinguishes between Fachbezogene (subject-specific) and Fachübergreifende Kompetenzspezifikation (cross-subject competency specification). By definition, a competency specification is part of an area and has a title.</p> <p>Learning content (CE-Lerninhalt) names concrete topics and subject matter through which competences are acquired. A learning content is part of an area or of another learning content.</p> <p>Note (CE-Hinweis) contains supplementary, recommending information: methodological suggestions, proposals for differentiation or ideas for deepening. A note is part of a competency specification, a learning content or an area.</p> <p>Reference (CE-Verweis, see Pattern 7) establishes a reference from one element to another.</p> <p>Guiding perspective (CE-Leitperspektive) describes overarching educational goals such as sustainability or media education that run through several subjects and class levels.</p> <p>The part-whole relationship</p> <p>The elements are linked to each other via has direct part (<code>LP_0000565</code>) or its inverse direct part of (direkt Teil von, <code>LP_0000566</code>): an element refers to its immediately subordinate elements. The order is given by hat Position (<code>LP_0000460</code>). Since has direct part is a sub-property of the transitive relation has part (hat Teil, <code>BFO_0000051</code>), all indirect parts can be derived from it – for example, all competency specifications of a curriculum, regardless of the depth of the structure.</p> <p>Typical hierarchies are:</p> <ul> <li>CE-Fragment → CE-Bereich → CE-Kompetenzspezifikation → CE-Hinweis</li> <li>CE-Fragment → CE-Bereich → CE-Bereich → CE-Kompetenzspezifikation</li> <li>CE-Fragment → CE-Bereich → CE-Lerninhalt → CE-Lerninhalt → CE-Hinweis</li> </ul> <p>A Bavarian curriculum, for example, is divided into elements of the class Lernbereich (BY) (learning area, Bavaria; an area), which contain elements of the classes Kompetenzerwartung (BY) (competence expectation, Bavaria; a competency specification) and Inhalt zu den Kompetenzen (BY) (content for the competences, Bavaria; a learning content). A Hamburg Bildungsplan uses Kompetenzbereich (HH) (competence area, Hamburg) and Anforderung (HH) (requirement, Hamburg) instead.</p>

+ − Fit ⛶ DagreForceCircle ConcentricTreeGrid LOD L0 · classes only L1 · + hierarchy L2 · + individuals &amp; object props L3 · + OWL restrictions L4 · + data props &amp; literals L5 · everything except inferred L6 · everything Hidden  Group Facets Style: Ontoink Style: Chowlk Style: Graffoo Style: VOWL PNG SVG TTL Edit Layout Abstract Stats Paths SPARQL Reasoning Edit &amp; Validate Hidden by LOD  ·  pin to reveal× Facets  ·  narrow the view× Suggested SHACL shapes× Cite this ontology× Inferred Triples (OWL-RL)×  Show on graph Validate with Inferences Edit &amp; Validate× Source (data TTL) SHACL Shapes Validation Report Validate Update Graph Reset <p>RDF data:</p> <pre><code>@prefix ex: &lt;https://www.example.org/&gt; .
@prefix owl: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#&gt; .
@prefix rdf: &lt;http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&gt; .
@prefix rdfs: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt; .

@prefix lp: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/&gt; .

# Klassen
@prefix Curriculares_Element: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000261&gt; .
@prefix CE_Bereich: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000349&gt; .
@prefix CE_Kompetenzspezifikation: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000263&gt; .
@prefix CE_Verweis: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030065&gt; .
@prefix Verweis_auf_Lernbereich_des_gleichen_Faches_einer_anderen_Klassenstufe_SN: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030189&gt; .

# properties
@prefix hat_verweis: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030071&gt; .
@prefix verweist_auf: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030072&gt; .
@prefix hat_beschreibung: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030051&gt; .

ex:kompetenz_1 a CE_Kompetenzspezifikation: ;
                hat_verweis: ex:verweis_1 .
ex:verweis_1 a Verweis_auf_Lernbereich_des_gleichen_Faches_einer_anderen_Klassenstufe_SN: ;
              verweist_auf: ex:lernbereich_1 ;
              hat_beschreibung: ex:beschreibung_1 .
ex:lernbereich_1 a CE_Bereich: .
CE_Kompetenzspezifikation: rdfs:subClassOf Curriculares_Element: .
Verweis_auf_Lernbereich_des_gleichen_Faches_einer_anderen_Klassenstufe_SN: rdfs:subClassOf CE_Verweis: .
</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>A reference (CE-Verweis, <code>LP_0030065</code>) is a curricular element that establishes a link from one element to another or to an external resource. The reference is not the target itself but the pointer to it: the source element carries the reference via has reference (hat Verweis, <code>LP_0030071</code>), the reference points to the target via refers to (verweist auf, <code>LP_0030072</code>) and can have its own description.</p> <p>A reference can point</p> <ul> <li>within the same curriculum, e.g. from one competence area to another ("see also learning area 3"),</li> <li>into another curriculum, e.g. across subjects from the German to the history curriculum,</li> <li>to external resources, e.g. educational standards of the KMK or materials.</li> </ul> <p>In the curriculum data, references appear as state-specific classes – in rc6 there are 47, e.g. Verweis auf standardillustrierende Aufgaben (BE) (reference to tasks illustrating the standards, Berlin), Verweis auf vernetzte Kompetenzen (BE) (reference to interlinked competences, Berlin) or Verweis auf Lernbereich des gleichen Faches einer anderen Klassenstufe (SN) (reference to a learning area of the same subject in another class level, Saxony). They carry the Verweisbeschreibungsfunktion (reference description function) and are therefore derived as subclasses of reference (see Pattern 8); in the example, this derived subclass relationship is drawn directly.</p> <p>Since cross-references are modeled not as free text but as typed elements, they can be analyzed: Which competence areas are linked to each other? How densely interlinked is a curriculum internally? Which subjects refer to each other?</p> <p>Provenance of references</p> <p>References do not always come from the curriculum document itself. They can also be added subsequently, for example by an AI system (AI: artificial intelligence) that automatically identifies elements with related content, or by an editorial team that defines links manually. For the assessment and maintenance of such references, it is important to record where they come from.</p> <p>This can be represented with the means of Basic Formal Ontology (BFO) and the Relation Ontology (RO), which the Curriculum Ontology already reuses: a reference is the output of a process (<code>BFO_0000015</code>, process), via output of (<code>RO_0002353</code>) or inversely has output (<code>RO_0002234</code>). The actor who created the reference participates in this process via has participant (<code>RO_0000057</code>): a person (Person, <code>LP_0000010</code>) or a technical system on which an AI method is executed.</p> <pre><code>@prefix ex:             &lt;https://www.example.org/&gt; .
@prefix CE_Verweis:     &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0030065&gt; .
@prefix Person:         &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000010&gt; .
@prefix Process:        &lt;http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015&gt; .
@prefix Object:         &lt;http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000030&gt; .
@prefix output_of:      &lt;http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002353&gt; .
@prefix hat_teilnehmer: &lt;http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057&gt; .

# automatisch durch ein KI-System ermittelter Verweis
ex:verweis_2 a CE_Verweis: ;
             output_of: ex:zuordnung_1 .
ex:zuordnung_1 a Process: ;
             hat_teilnehmer: ex:ki_system_1 .
ex:ki_system_1 a Object: .

# von einer Person angegebener Verweis
ex:verweis_3 a CE_Verweis: ;
             output_of: ex:zuordnung_2 .
ex:zuordnung_2 a Process: ;
             hat_teilnehmer: ex:redakteurin_1 .
ex:redakteurin_1 a Person: .
</code></pre> <p>On this basis, references from the curriculum itself can be distinguished from subsequently added ones, automatically identified references can be checked before they are adopted, and they can be filtered selectively if needed.</p> <p>In version rc6, the Curriculum Ontology does not yet contain specific classes for such processes. For a simple distinction in the data, separate subclasses of process suggest themselves, for example for automatic and editorial assignments. It is also still open how the time and reliability of an automatic assignment, such as a confidence value, are to be specified.</p>

