@prefix owl: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#&gt; .
@prefix rdf: &lt;http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&gt; .
@prefix rdfs: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt; .

@prefix lp: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/&gt; .

# Klassen
@prefix Funktionsspezifikation: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000478&gt; .
@prefix Beschreibungsfunktion: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000493&gt; .
@prefix Strukturierungsfunktion: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000482&gt; .
@prefix Curriculares_Element: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000261&gt; .
@prefix Element_NW: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0002085&gt; .
@prefix Kompetenzerwartung_NW: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0002188&gt; .
@prefix Kompetenzbereich_NW: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0002187&gt; .
@prefix CE_Bereich: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000349&gt; .
@prefix CE_Kompetenzspezifikation: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000263&gt; .

# Individuen
@prefix kompetenzbeschreibungsfunktion: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000479&gt; .
@prefix bereichsfunktion: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000497&gt; .

# properties
@prefix hat_funktion: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000483&gt; .

ex:kompetenz_1 a Kompetenzerwartung_NW: ,
               CE_Kompetenzspezifikation: ;
             hat_funktion: kompetenzbeschreibungsfunktion: .
Kompetenzerwartung_NW: rdfs:subClassOf Element_NW: .
CE_Kompetenzspezifikation: rdfs:subClassOf Curriculares_Element: .
kompetenzbeschreibungsfunktion: a Beschreibungsfunktion: .                       
Beschreibungsfunktion: rdfs:subClassOf Funktionsspezifikation: . 
ex:bereich_1 a Kompetenzbereich_NW: ,
             CE_Bereich: ;
           hat_funktion: bereichsfunktion: . 
Kompetenzbereich_NW: rdfs:subClassOf Element_NW: .
CE_Bereich: rdfs:subClassOf Curriculares_Element: .
bereichsfunktion: a Strukturierungsfunktion: .                       
Strukturierungsfunktion: rdfs:subClassOf Funktionsspezifikation: .
Element_NW: rdfs:subClassOf Curriculares_Element: .
</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>The problem: many names, one meaning</p> <p>The states have structured their curricula very differently and use their own terms. What is called Lernbereich in Bavaria is called Kompetenzbereich in Hamburg, Kompetenzbereich, Leitidee or Thema in Rhineland-Palatinate, and likewise Lernbereich in Saxony. Without a mapping mechanism, a nationwide query would require knowing each of the more than 400 state-specific classes.</p> <p>The solution: function specifications</p> <p>In rc6, each state-specific class is defined as a subclass of an intersection: of the Element (XX) class of its state and a fixed function, which refers via has function specification (hat Funktion, <code>LP_0000483</code>) to an individual of the class function specification (Funktionsspezifikation, <code>LP_0000478</code>). There are three kinds of functions:</p> <p>The Strukturierungsfunktion (structuring function, <code>LP_0000482</code>) describes how an element structures the curriculum:</p> <ul> <li>Fragmentfunktion (fragment function) – purely structuring component (chapter, section). This function is carried by the 16 classes Lehrplanfragment (XX).</li> <li>Bereichsfunktion (area function) – division into subject-related coherent areas. 119 classes carry this function, including Kompetenzbereich (HH), Lernbereich (BY), Leitidee (BE) and Inhaltsfeld (HE).</li> </ul> <p>The Beschreibungsfunktion (description function, <code>LP_0000493</code>) describes what an element accomplishes in terms of content:</p> <ul> <li>Kompetenzbeschreibungsfunktion (competence description function) – formulates a competence to be acquired, e.g. Anforderung (HH), Kompetenzerwartung (BY), Kompetenz (RP), Standard (BE) → competency specification</li> <li>Lerninhaltsbeschreibungsfunktion (learning content description function) – names a learning subject matter → learning content</li> <li>Hinweisbeschreibungsfunktion (note description function) – contains a methodological or didactic note, e.g. Bemerkung (SN) (remark, Saxony), Hinweis und Anregung (MV) (note and suggestion, Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania) → note</li> <li>Verweisbeschreibungsfunktion (reference description function) – refers to another element → reference</li> <li>Leitperspektivenbeschreibungsfunktion (guiding perspective description function) – describes an overarching guiding perspective → guiding perspective</li> <li>Materialbeschreibungsfunktion (material description function) – describes learning or additional material, e.g. learning material (BE) (Lernmaterial (BE))</li> </ul> <p>The Bezugsfunktion (relation function, <code>LP_0000499</code>) additionally specifies what an element relates to in terms of content. It always occurs in combination with one of the other functions:</p> <ul> <li>Prozessbezugsfunktion (process relation function) – process-related competences (how learning or acting takes place), e.g. Prozessbezogene Kompetenz (NI) (process-related competence, Lower Saxony)</li> <li>Inhaltsbezugsfunktion (content relation function) – content-related competences (what is learned), e.g. Leitidee (BW) (guiding idea, Baden-Württemberg)</li> <li>Domänenbezugsfunktion (domain relation function) – relation to a subject domain</li> </ul> <p>In addition, the class function specification contains the individuals Verbindlich (mandatory) and Optional (optional).</p> <p>How the mapping works technically</p> <pre><code>@prefix rdfs:                 &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt; .
@prefix owl:                  &lt;http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#&gt; .
@prefix Lernbereich_BY:       &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0002046&gt; .
@prefix Element_BY:           &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000434&gt; .
@prefix CE_Bereich:           &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000349&gt; .
@prefix Curriculares_Element: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000261&gt; .
@prefix hat_funktion:         &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000483&gt; .
@prefix bereichsfunktion:     &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000497&gt; .

Lernbereich_BY:
  rdfs:subClassOf [
    owl:intersectionOf (
      Element_BY:
      [ owl:onProperty hat_funktion: ;
        owl:hasValue   bereichsfunktion: ]
    )
  ] .

CE_Bereich:
  owl:equivalentClass [
    owl:intersectionOf (
      Curriculares_Element:
      [ owl:onProperty hat_funktion: ;
        owl:hasValue   bereichsfunktion: ]
    )
  ] .
</code></pre> <p>Every instance of Lernbereich (BY) thus automatically has the area function – without an explicit has function specification triple having to be present in the curriculum data. Since area is defined as exactly this combination, a reasoner classifies Lernbereich (BY) as a subclass of area.</p> <p>For competency specification, learning content and note, the definition additionally requires embedding in the structure (see Pattern 6). These classes are therefore derived not at class level but for each individual element in the data. The example shows the result: the element is at the same time Kompetenzerwartung (NW) (competence expectation, North Rhine-Westphalia) and competency specification and carries the competence description function.</p> <p>What this means for queries</p> <p>In the SPARQL endpoint (SPARQL: SPARQL Protocol and RDF Query Language), the triples derived by the reasoner are available in separate graphs (see SPARQL queries). This makes it possible to query nationwide without knowing the state-specific classes:</p> <ul> <li>"All competence areas from all states" → all instances of area or with has function specification → Bereichsfunktion</li> <li>"All requirements from the Hamburg German curriculum" → all instances with has function specification → Kompetenzbeschreibungsfunktion, filtered on Hamburg</li> <li>"All notes" → all instances with has function specification → Hinweisbeschreibungsfunktion</li> </ul> <p>The function specifications are thus the central bridge between the terminology of the states and a uniform, nationwide semantics.</p>

