</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>Niveau (niveau, level; <code>LP_0000037</code>) is the superclass of all performance and requirement levels. It is divided into four subclasses.</p> <p>The educational track level (<code>LP_0000028</code>) describes the performance standard with which content and competences are formulated for a particular learning group – and thus toward which school-leaving qualification teaching is directed. There are five generic level classes: Grundschulniveau (primary school level), Hauptschulniveau (Hauptschule level), Realschulniveau (Realschule level), Gymnasialniveau Sek I (Gymnasium level, lower secondary) and Gymnasialniveau Sek II (Gymnasium level, upper secondary). For each state there is also a class Bildungsgangniveau (XX) (educational track level of state XX), defined as an educational track level with of federal state = XX. The concrete levels of the states are individuals that belong to one or more generic classes and to the class of their state.</p> <p>The names vary considerably: the Hauptschule level is called Mittelschulniveau in Bavaria and Mindestanforderungen (minimum requirements) in Hamburg; the Regelschulniveau (TH) and the Sekundarstufenniveau (SH) cover several levels at once. The Gymnasium level Sek I is called Erweitertes Anforderungsniveau (extended requirement level) in Bremen, Erhöhtes Kompetenzniveau (increased competence level) in Rhineland-Palatinate and Erweiterungskurs (extension course) in North Rhine-Westphalia. Berlin and Brandenburg differentiate by qualification and niveau stage, e.g. MSA A–G for the mittlerer Schulabschluss (MSA, intermediate school-leaving certificate) or Gymnasialniveau Sek I A–H (see Pattern 11).</p> <p>The Fachniveau Sek II (subject level, upper secondary, <code>LP_0000265</code>) describes the course type in the upper level of the Gymnasium. It has the generic subclasses Grundkursniveau (basic course level) and Leistungskursniveau (advanced course level). The course types of the states are individuals of these classes and of the class Fachniveau Sek II (XX) of their state, e.g. Grundlegendes Anforderungsniveau (ST) (basic requirement level, Saxony-Anhalt) or Leistungskursfach (BB) (advanced course subject, Brandenburg).</p> <p>The Anforderungsbereich (requirement area, <code>LP_0000802</code>) comes from the KMK educational standards and classifies the cognitive demand of a task or competence. The three individuals are Anforderungsbereich 1 (Reproduktion) (requirement area 1, reproduction), Anforderungsbereich 2 (Reorganisation und Transfer) (requirement area 2, reorganization and transfer) and Anforderungsbereich 3 (Reflexion und Problemlösung) (requirement area 3, reflection and problem solving). Unlike educational track levels and subject levels, it describes not organizational conditions but the cognitive depth of a learning objective – independent of school type or state.</p> <p>The Fremdsprachenniveau (foreign language level, <code>LP_0010001</code>) represents the six levels of the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages (Gemeinsamer Europäischer Referenzrahmen für Sprachen, GER), from A1 Anfänger (A1 beginner, <code>LP_0030317</code>) to C2 Annähernd muttersprachliche Kenntnisse (C2 near-native proficiency, <code>LP_0030313</code>). These levels are uniform nationwide and make it possible to link curriculum elements from foreign language subjects to the GER.</p>

