</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>Educational tracks, educational track levels and qualifications together describe the framework within which curriculum content applies: at which level of demand learning takes place and what the school career is aimed at. As everywhere in the ontology, a distinction is made between the real-world entity and the information unit that describes it.</p> <p>Educational track specification (Bildungsgangspezifikation, <code>LP_0000816</code>) describes a school career that leads to a particular qualification. The three generic subclasses Gymnasium track (Gymnasialer Bildungsgang), Realschule track (Realschulbildungsgang) and Hauptschule track (Hauptschulbildungsgang) are defined via their educational track level – a Realschule track is exactly an educational track specification with Realschule level. The educational track (Bildungsgang, <code>LP_0000567</code>) itself is the process that a person goes through according to this specification. An educational track is not the same as a school type: the Gymnasium track can also be completed at a Gesamtschule (comprehensive school) or Gemeinschaftsschule.</p> <p>Educational track level (<code>LP_0000028</code>) describes the performance standard within an educational track (see Pattern 9). In the curriculum data, it is attached to curricula and individual elements via has educational track level (<code>LP_0000833</code>) to specify for which learning group a competence applies.</p> <p>School-leaving qualification specification (Schulabschlussspezifikation, <code>LP_0000019</code>) describes a school-leaving qualification and the requirements for its award. The generic subclasses are defined via the required level:</p> <ul> <li>Erster Schulabschluss (first school-leaving qualification) – requires level (benötigt Niveau) some Hauptschulniveau</li> <li>Mittlerer Schulabschluss (intermediate school-leaving qualification) – requires level some Realschulniveau</li> <li>Allgemeine Hochschulreife (general higher education entrance qualification) – requires level some Gymnasialniveau Sek II</li> </ul> <p>For each state there are subclasses such as Mittlerer Abschluss (RP) (intermediate qualification, Rhineland-Palatinate), whose individuals are the concrete qualifications, e.g. Qualifizierter Sekundarabschluss I (RP) (qualified lower secondary qualification, Rhineland-Palatinate). The school-leaving qualification role (Schulabschluss, <code>LP_0000008</code>) itself is the role that a person receives upon attaining it. An educational track specification refers via leads to qualification (ermöglicht Abschluss, <code>LP_0000021</code>) to the attainable school-leaving qualification specification.</p> <p>The concepts form a chain:</p> <pre><code>Realschulbildungsgang
   ──[hat Bildungsgangniveau]──▶ Realschulniveau
   ──[ermöglicht Abschluss]────▶ Mittlerer Schulabschluss
                                    ──[benötigt Niveau]──▶ Realschulniveau
</code></pre> <p>In the example, the required level is specified directly on the Rhineland-Palatinate qualification. In rc6, it is fixed as a class axiom on Mittlerer Schulabschluss and thus applies to all intermediate qualifications.</p> <p>For curriculum data this means: a competency specification with <code>has educational track level → Gymnasialniveau Sek I</code> applies to learners in the Gymnasium track of lower secondary level – regardless of whether they attend a Gymnasium or a Gesamtschule.</p>

