jahrgangsstufe_6: a Jahrgangsstufe: .
jahrgangsstufe_7: a Jahrgangsstufe: .
jahrgangsstufe_8: a Jahrgangsstufe: .
</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>Berlin and Brandenburg work with joint Rahmenlehrpläne (framework curricula). These structure competences not primarily by class levels but along eight niveau stages A to H (Niveaustufen), which represent different degrees of competence development. In the ontology, they are individuals of the class Niveaustufe BE/BB (niveau stage, Berlin/Brandenburg, <code>LP_0000443</code>).</p> <p>Competency specifications, e.g. standard (BE) (Standard (BE)), are assigned to a niveau stage via has niveau stage (hat Niveaustufe, <code>LP_0000578</code>); the inverse is is niveau stage of (ist Niveaustufe von, <code>LP_0000580</code>). However, the niveau stage alone is not sufficient for comparability, because a competence must always be read in the context of the targeted qualification.</p> <p>The concretization is therefore done via educational track levels that combine niveau stage and qualification: in Berlin there is a series of levels for each qualification type – BOA A–E, BBR A–F, EBBR A–G, MSA A–G and Gymnasialniveau Sek I A–H –, and in Brandenburg correspondingly EBR A–G, FOR A–G and FOR-Q A–H. The abbreviations denote the targeted qualifications: in Berlin the berufsorientierender Abschluss (BOA, career-oriented qualification), the Berufsbildungsreife (BBR, basic vocational qualification), the erweiterte Berufsbildungsreife (EBBR, extended basic vocational qualification) and the mittlerer Schulabschluss (MSA); in Brandenburg the erweiterte Berufsbildungsreife (EBR, extended basic vocational qualification), the Fachoberschulreife (FOR, entrance qualification for upper vocational school) and the Fachoberschulreife mit Berechtigung zum Besuch der gymnasialen Oberstufe (FOR-Q, FOR with entitlement to attend the upper secondary level of the Gymnasium). Each of these levels refers via is niveau of (ist Niveau von, <code>LP_0000086</code>) to its niveau stage; conversely, the niveau stage has all associated levels via has niveau (hat Niveau, <code>LP_0000840</code>). The levels are individuals of classes such as MSA Niveau (MSA level), which are defined both as an educational track level of the state and as a generic level (MSA Niveau as Realschulniveau in Berlin).</p> <p>To make the BE/BB levels comparable with the other states, each level carries via has class level (<code>LP_0000026</code>) the class levels in which it is typically reached. The assignment deliberately overlaps, because the Rahmenlehrplan provides for individual learning development instead of rigid boundaries. Across all qualification types, the following ranges result in rc6:</p> Niveau stage Class levels A 1–2 B 1–3 C 2–7 D 4–9 E 6–10 F 7–10 G 9–10 H 10 <p>The exact class levels depend on the qualification type; MSA E, for example, lies in class levels 6–8.</p> <p>In summary: the BE/BB Rahmenlehrplan links competency specifications with niveau stages. The combination of niveau stage and targeted qualification yields the educational track level, via which in turn the class levels can be determined. Comparability with the other states rests on two mechanisms:</p> <ol> <li>Generic educational track levels: the qualification-specific levels (e.g. MSA) belong to the generic level classes (e.g. Realschulniveau).</li> <li>Common class levels: since all states use the same class level IRIs, requirements can be compared nationwide.</li> </ol>

