</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>Curricula apply for a certain period: they come into force at the start of a school year and are later replaced by new versions. Two mechanisms are available for this information:</p> <ul> <li>veröffentlicht am (published on, <code>LP_0000553</code>) specifies the publication date of a curriculum.</li> <li>has validity scope (<code>LP_0000550</code>) refers to a validity scope (Gültigkeitsbereich, <code>LP_0000547</code>), which describes the temporal scope. It carries the start and end of validity via von Datum (from date, <code>LP_0000548</code>) and to date (bis Datum, <code>LP_0000549</code>).</li> </ul> <p>All dates have the data type <code>xsd:dateTimeStamp</code> and are sub-properties of has value.</p> <p>A validity scope is a separate information unit and can therefore be shared by several curricula. This is the usual case when a state puts the curricula of several subjects or class levels into force on the same date. In the example, the curricula for German and mathematics refer to the same validity scope. If the period changes, for example because a transition period is extended, an adjustment in one place is sufficient.</p> <p>Not yet in the curriculum data</p> <p>The classes and properties are defined in rc6 but are not yet used in the curriculum data.</p>

