@prefix CE_Kompetenzspezifikation: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000263&gt; .

# properties
@prefix hat_rolle: &lt;http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000087&gt; .
@prefix hat_eigenschaft: &lt;http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053&gt; .
@prefix hat_teilnehmer: &lt;http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057&gt; .
@prefix hat_output: &lt;http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002234&gt; .
@prefix occurs_in: &lt;http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000066&gt; .
@prefix ist_teil_von: &lt;http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050&gt; .
@prefix wird_beschrieben_von: &lt;https://w3id.org/lehrplan/ontology/LP_0000024&gt; .

ex:schuelerin_1 a Person: ;
               hat_rolle: ex:schuelerrolle_1 ;
               hat_eigenschaft: ex:kompetenz_1 .
ex:schuelerrolle_1 a Schueler_Rolle: .

ex:lehrkraft_1 a Person: ;
             hat_rolle: ex:lehrerrolle_1 .
ex:lehrerrolle_1 a Lehrer_Rolle: .

ex:unterricht_1 a Lehrprozess: ;
              hat_teilnehmer: ex:lehrkraft_1 , ex:schuelerin_1 ;
              ist_teil_von: ex:bildungsgang_1 .

ex:lernprozess_1 a Lernprozess: ;
               hat_teilnehmer: ex:schuelerin_1 ;
               occurs_in: ex:schuelerin_1 ;
               hat_output: ex:kompetenz_1 .

ex:kompetenz_1 a Kompetenz: ;
             wird_beschrieben_von: ex:kompetenzerwartung_1 .
ex:kompetenzerwartung_1 a CE_Kompetenzspezifikation: .

ex:bildungsgang_1 a Bildungsgang: ;
                hat_teilnehmer: ex:schuelerin_1 ;
                wird_beschrieben_von: ex:realschulbildungsgang_1 .
ex:realschulbildungsgang_1 a Realschulbildungsgang: .
</code></pre> <p>Explanation:</p> <p>The previous patterns describe curricula as information units: they specify which competences are to be acquired. This pattern shows how actual teaching and the learning of individual persons can be connected to them. It takes up the distinction between real-world entities and the information units that describe them (see Basic ontological understanding).</p> <p>Persons and roles</p> <p>Students and teachers are instances of the class person (Person, <code>LP_0000010</code>). Their function in teaching is not a separate kind of person but a role that a person bears: the student role (Schüler Rolle, <code>LP_0000012</code>) or the teacher role (Lehrer Rolle, <code>LP_0000011</code>). Person and role are connected via has role (<code>RO_0000087</code>). The same person can thus take on different roles over time.</p> <p>Teaching process and learning process</p> <p>The teaching process (Lehrprozess, <code>LP_0000006</code>) is a planned process in which persons participate in the role of teachers and learners, such as a lesson. The learning process (Lernprozess, <code>LP_0000007</code>), by contrast, takes place in the learning person themselves; this is expressed via occurs in (<code>BFO_0000066</code>). It can be triggered by a teaching process but is not identical to it: not all teaching leads to learning, and learning also takes place outside of teaching. Persons participate in both processes via has participant (<code>RO_0000057</code>). The relation occurs in is not yet included in rc6 and must be imported into the Curriculum Ontology from BFO or the Relation Ontology for this pattern.</p> <p>Competence as a result</p> <p>The result of a successful learning process is a competence (Kompetenz, <code>LP_0000013</code>). It is a characteristic of the learning person, not information: the person bears it via has characteristic (<code>RO_0000053</code>). In the example, the competence is specified as the result of the learning process via has output (<code>RO_0002234</code>). The connection to the curriculum is established by described by (<code>LP_0000024</code>): the competence of a concrete person is described by a competency specification in the curriculum, such as a competence expectation. According to the definition in rc6, every competence is described by at least one competency specification.</p> <p>Embedding in the educational track</p> <p>Teaching is part of an educational track (<code>LP_0000567</code>) via ist Teil von (part of, <code>BFO_0000050</code>), i.e. of the school career that a person goes through. The learning process, by contrast, is not part of the educational track: it takes place in the learning person and is not bound to the organizational framework of the school career. The educational track is described by an educational track specification, in the example a Realschule track (see Pattern 10).</p> <pre><code>Lehrplan ──[hat Teil]──▶ CE-Kompetenzspezifikation
                                  ▲
                      [wird beschrieben von]
                                  │
Person ──[has characteristic]──▶ Kompetenz ◀──[has output]── Lernprozess
</code></pre> <p>Not yet in the curriculum data</p> <p>The classes and relations of this pattern are defined in rc6 but are not used in the curriculum data: the curriculum data describe requirements, not actual teaching. The pattern shows how data on teaching, learning progress or educational trajectories, for example from learning platforms, can be connected to the curriculum data. Personal data are subject to data protection requirements.</p>

